#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
"""Monban conformance runner (P6-conformance-001, P8-conformance-001; PLAN-6 D8; PREFLIGHT D-P8.5; ARCHITECTURE
R-ASSURE-2 C0-C4; frozen interface F13).

Usage:
  conformance/run [--logs gates/out/logs] [--out gates/out/conformance] [--toml gates/phase-N.toml] [--gate NAME]
                  [--require C0,C1,C2[,C3][,C4]] [--config-pin]
  conformance/run --self-test [same mode flags]

What it does. It reads the gate logs of the current run, maps the gates to conformance levels, writes one F13 report
per subject to <out>/<subject>.json, triple-signs each report with per-run throwaway test keys, validates each report
against interfaces/F13-conformance-report.schema.json and verifies the signatures back. The gate passes iff, for every
golden subject (monban-bin floor and monban-bin cmvp), every REQUIRED level is 100% (passed == total), every subject's
report could be written, validated and verified, and (with --config-pin) every golden subject passes the config pin.
Levels that are not required are reported, not gated. Without --require the required set is C0,C1,C2 (the Phase 6/7
gate `conformance`); gate `conformance-full` (Phase 8, R3) passes --require C0,C1,C2,C3,C4 --config-pin.

Which run. --toml defaults to gates/phase-N.toml with N from the <logs>/.run-start `phase=N` line (a real run with
no such line FAILs; --self-test falls back to the highest-numbered toml); logs are <logs>/phaseN-<gate>-<step>.log,
and a log is judged only when the marker's phase equals the toml's.
The conformance gate itself ("this gate") is the toml gate whose cmd (selftest, under --self-test) is exactly this
invocation (`[python3 -I] conformance/run <same args>`), or --gate NAME. Every member of a required level, every
digest gate and every TRACE gate must be a gate of the toml placed before this gate: the runner refuses to start
otherwise (a gate that runs later can never have a log from this run). A member of a level that is not required may
run later; it is then judged fail ("runs after this gate").

Level map (real gate names; `g[o]` = oracle o judged inside aggregate gate g by its `[o] ...` lines):
  C0 static      fips-lock budget layering no-cedar-in-bin no-wasmtime-in-bin unsafe-sites panic-abort
                 config-totality; cmvp adds cmvp-client-policy and fips-binary
  C1 behavioural tls-verdicts h2-conformance transport-limits reverse-proxy-e2e kx-interop kx-kat;
                 cmvp adds clienthello-cmvp
  C2 adversarial p2-hostile-host p2-hostile-worker mcp-gateway oracles-remote[ssrf-corpus]
  C3 model DRT   select-drt oracles-local[token-drt] oracles-remote[pdp-dst] lowering-read-{sqlite,pg,redis,mariadb,
                 crdb} lowering-write-{sqlite,pg,redis,mariadb,crdb} (D-P8.5: every DRT gate, 0 divergence)
  C4 trace       every F1 statement id of spec/STATEMENTS.sha256, through spec/TRACE.toml, plus the TRACE file itself
  monban-p2 (kind module; the P2 worker that hosts guest modules): C2 only (p2-hostile-worker, p2-hostile-host).

When a gate counts as passed (anything else is fail; a result is never "skipped"):
  - <logs>/.run-start exists (ci/run-gates.py writes it at the start of a run);
  - <logs>/phaseN-<gate>-cmd.log exists, is a regular file, its mtime is strictly newer than .run-start, it starts
    with `$ <cmd>` where <cmd> is the gate's cmd from the toml (plain, or wrapped by run-gates.py for remote gates),
    and its last line is exactly `[exit 0]` (run-gates.py writes `$ cmd\\n<output>\\n[exit N]\\n`);
  - if the gate has a selftest in the toml, <logs>/phaseN-<gate>-selftest.log meets the same conditions;
  - an embedded member g[o] also needs `[o] <NAME>: PASS` in g's cmd log and `[o] <NAME> SELF-TEST: PASS` in its
    selftest log.
  log_sha256 = sha256 of the cmd log file bytes (sha256 of the empty string when the log is missing; the reason says
  so); the selftest log's sha256 is given in `reason`.

C3 (D-P8.5). A DRT member passes only if it passes as above AND its cmd log carries at least one verdict line of its
oracle, and every such line is PASS with 0 divergence read from the line itself (an exit code alone is not enough):
  select-drt      `SELECT-DRT: PASS (P profiles x n cases = N, seed s, D divergence;` P = the 8 F8 profiles, N > 0,
                  D = 0, and no `DIVERGE ` line
  token-drt       `[token-drt] TOKEN-DRT: PASS (N cases, D divergences)`  N > 0, D = 0
  pdp-dst         `[pdp-dst] PDP-DST: PASS (N cases match Cedar, F faulted exchanges all ERROR->DENY`  N, F > 0
                  (the oracle's divergence is a violation; any violation prints FAIL)
  lowering-read-* `LOWERING-READ: PASS (cases=N ... leak= widen= miss= errors= unrefused=)` N > 0, all others 0
  lowering-write-* `LOWERING-WRITE: PASS (cases=N ... W1= W2= W4= W6= W7= E= FORM= REFUSE= BIND= ACL=)` N > 0, others 0
  A missing counter is a fail (an oracle whose verdict format changed is not judged by guesswork).

C4 (D-P8.5). spec/TRACE.toml: `v = 1`, `ledger = "spec/STATEMENTS.sha256"`, `ledger_sha256` = sha256 of that file,
and a [trace] table: statement id -> non-empty list of gate ids (a gate name or a known embedded member). The TRACE
member passes iff the file parses, the ledger pin matches, every row id is a ledger id, every listed gate exists and
runs before this gate, and the list is non-empty. A statement passes iff it has a row and every gate in it passes
(cmd + selftest logs from this run, as above). C4 = (statements passed + TRACE ok) / (statements + 1).

Config pin (--config-pin; D-P8.5). conformance/config-pin.toml pins, per golden subject, the effective-config hash
(monban-config config_hash) of its golden config. Evidence: lines `CONFORMANCE-BOOT: <subject> artifact A config H`
(printed by conformance/boot-pin, which boots the artifact with the golden config) in the passing cmd log of any
gate placed before this gate. The pin passes iff the pin is a 64-hex value, at least one line exists for the
subject, and every line has H == the pin and A == the subject's artifact_sha256. Otherwise the subject's report is
REFUSED (not written; an earlier one is removed) and the gate fails. A passing report carries
`config_sha256` = the pin. The module subject is not pinned.

Artifact digest (artifact_sha256). Taken only from logs that themselves pass the rule above:
  - golden floor / cmvp: the line `RELEASE-PIPELINE: PASS (<profile>, artifacts/monban-<profile> sha256 <hex>, ...)`
    that ci/release/pipeline.sh prints, found in the cmd logs of release-verify (floor) and release-rebuild (floor,
    cmvp) and in the subject's own gate logs;
  - any subject: a line `CONFORMANCE-ARTIFACT: <subject> sha256 <hex>` in those same logs (monban-p2 has no other
    source: the p2-hostile-* gates must print it for the module build they exercised).
  Every digest found for a subject must be identical; none found, or two different ones, fails the subject (no
  report can be written, since F13 requires artifact_sha256) and therefore the gate.

Signatures (F13 `signatures`, PREFLIGHT D-P2). Message = the report without `signatures`, serialized as
json.dumps(obj, sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':'), ensure_ascii=False) and encoded as UTF-8. The three keys
(Ed25519, SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s, ML-DSA-87) are generated per run with /usr/bin/openssl (>= 3.5) in a mktemp dir on the
signing host ($AEGIS_CONFORMANCE_SIGN_HOST, default kamrui; `local` runs the same script here), which is removed
before the session ends. Only messages go over ssh (stdin) and only public keys and signatures come back; no private
key ever leaves that temp dir. Reports carry "test_keys": true. The public keys are written to <out>/keys/<alg>.pub.pem.
Verification sends public keys, messages and signatures to the same host (`openssl pkeyutl -verify -rawin`) and
checks each key's type; a report is accepted only if all three verify (REL-1).

Schema validation: a strict hand-written validator for exactly F13 always runs; when the `jsonschema` package is
importable, Draft 2020-12 validation with the format checker runs as well, and both must accept. F13 members added
2026-11-06 (additive, v stays 1): `config_sha256`, `gated`.

Output: one line per gate per subject, one SUBJECT line per subject, last line
  CONFORMANCE: PASS (...)  /  CONFORMANCE: FAIL (...)            exit 0 / 1 (2 = usage)
  CONFORMANCE SELF-TEST: PASS (...)  /  CONFORMANCE SELF-TEST: FAIL (...)
--self-test builds synthetic log directories in a temp dir (removed afterwards) from the real toml, judged as this
gate with this invocation's mode, and checks the real files (level map, spec/TRACE.toml against the real ledger and
toml, conformance/config-pin.toml structure, conformance/boot-pin --self-test) plus these mutants: all-pass is PASS; a
fork subject built with tls-client on in cmvp fails C0; a missing log, a stale log, a failing selftest log, a missing
.run-start, a missing or conflicting artifact digest, a wrong command line in a log, and a missing ssrf-corpus line
each fail; DRT logs with divergence 1 (select-drt, token-drt, lowering-write), a DRT FAIL verdict under [exit 0]
(pdp-dst), a missing divergence counter, a missing DRT verdict line, a DIVERGE line, and a stale DRT log each fail C3;
a statement without a TRACE row, a TRACE row for an unknown id, a TRACE gate that is not a gate, a TRACE gate placed
after this gate, a stale ledger pin, and a mapped gate without a log from this run each fail C4; a boot with a
different effective-config hash, a boot of a different artifact, no boot record, conflicting boot records and an
unpinned subject each refuse the report; the same C3 mutant passes when C3 is not required; a report tampered after
signing, and a report with one signature swapped, fail signature verification; schema mutants are rejected.
"""

import argparse
import base64
import binascii
import datetime
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import tomllib

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
SCHEMA = os.path.join(ROOT, "interfaces", "F13-conformance-report.schema.json")
F8 = os.path.join(ROOT, "interfaces", "F8-config.schema.json")
TRACE = os.path.join(ROOT, "spec", "TRACE.toml")
LEDGER_REL = "spec/STATEMENTS.sha256"
PINS = os.path.join(ROOT, "conformance", "config-pin.toml")
BOOT_PIN = os.path.join(ROOT, "conformance", "boot-pin")
ALGS = ("ed25519", "slh-dsa-sha2-128s", "ml-dsa-87")
OSSL_ALG = {"ed25519": "ED25519", "slh-dsa-sha2-128s": "SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s", "ml-dsa-87": "ML-DSA-87"}
SIG_LEN = {"ed25519": 64, "slh-dsa-sha2-128s": 7856, "ml-dsa-87": 4627}
EMPTY_SHA = hashlib.sha256(b"").hexdigest()
HEX64 = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{64}$")
LEVELS = ("C0", "C1", "C2", "C3", "C4")
LEGACY_REQUIRED = ("C0", "C1", "C2")

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- level map

C0_COMMON = ["fips-lock", "budget", "layering", "no-cedar-in-bin", "no-wasmtime-in-bin", "unsafe-sites",
             "panic-abort", "config-totality"]
C0_CMVP = ["cmvp-client-policy", "fips-binary"]
C1_COMMON = ["tls-verdicts", "h2-conformance", "transport-limits", "reverse-proxy-e2e", "kx-interop", "kx-kat"]
C1_CMVP = ["clienthello-cmvp"]
SSRF = "oracles-remote[ssrf-corpus]"
TOKEN = "oracles-local[token-drt]"
PDP = "oracles-remote[pdp-dst]"
C2_COMMON = ["p2-hostile-host", "p2-hostile-worker", "mcp-gateway", SSRF]
ENGINES = ("sqlite", "pg", "redis", "mariadb", "crdb")
LOWER_READ = [f"lowering-read-{e}" for e in ENGINES]
LOWER_WRITE = [f"lowering-write-{e}" for e in ENGINES]
C3_COMMON = ["select-drt", TOKEN, PDP] + LOWER_READ + LOWER_WRITE
# Members carried inside another gate's log: member -> (gate, cmd-log line regex, selftest-log line regex).
EMBEDDED = {
    SSRF: ("oracles-remote", r"^\[ssrf-corpus\] SSRF-CORPUS: PASS\b", r"^\[ssrf-corpus\] SSRF-CORPUS SELF-TEST: PASS\b"),
    TOKEN: ("oracles-local", r"^\[token-drt\] TOKEN-DRT: PASS\b", r"^\[token-drt\] TOKEN-DRT SELF-TEST: PASS\b"),
    PDP: ("oracles-remote", r"^\[pdp-dst\] PDP-DST: PASS\b", r"^\[pdp-dst\] PDP-DST SELF-TEST: PASS\b"),
}
DIGEST_GATES = ["release-verify", "release-rebuild"]
TRACE_MEMBER = "spec/TRACE.toml"
CONFIG_PIN_MEMBER = "config-pin"
NOTES = [
    "ssrf-corpus, token-drt, pdp-dst: no dedicated gates; judged inside oracles-remote / oracles-local by their [name] "
    "lines",
    "C4 traces the Lean statement ledger spec/STATEMENTS.sha256 (spec/TRACE.toml); SPEC_INVARIANTS.md prose clauses "
    "name their own gates",
]


def levels_for(profile):
    if profile == "module":
        return {"C2": ["p2-hostile-worker", "p2-hostile-host"]}
    cm = profile == "cmvp"
    return {"C0": C0_COMMON + (C0_CMVP if cm else []), "C1": C1_COMMON + (C1_CMVP if cm else []),
            "C2": list(C2_COMMON), "C3": list(C3_COMMON), "C4": None}  # C4 members come from spec/TRACE.toml


GOLDEN = [("monban-bin-floor", "golden", "floor"), ("monban-bin-cmvp", "golden", "cmvp")]
SUBJECTS = GOLDEN + [("monban-p2", "module", "module")]


class Mode:
    """How this invocation judges: the required levels, whether the config pin is on, and which gate it is."""

    def __init__(self, required, config_pin, self_gate, trace=TRACE, pins=PINS):
        self.required, self.config_pin, self.self_gate = tuple(required), bool(config_pin), self_gate
        self.trace, self.pins = trace, pins

    def gated(self, profile):
        return [L for L in LEVELS if L in self.required and L in levels_for(profile)]


def not_claimed(profile, mode):
    req = set(mode.required)
    nc = []
    rep = [L for L in ("C3", "C4") if L not in req]
    if profile == "module":
        nc.append("C0, C1, C3 and C4: the module subject is judged only at C2 (hostile-module corpus)")
        nc.append("config pin: the module subject is not pinned (its config is the host's)")
    else:
        if rep:
            nc.append(f"{' and '.join(rep)} {'is' if len(rep) == 1 else 'are'} reported, not gated, by this gate "
                      f"(gate conformance-full requires C0-C4)")
        nc.append("C3 is differential testing of the Rust code against the Lean models (R2 correspondence) and C4 is "
                  "traceability of the Lean statement ledger to gates: neither proves the Rust code")
        nc.append("C4 traces spec/STATEMENTS.sha256 only; the prose clauses of spec/SPEC_INVARIANTS.md are not traced")
        if mode.config_pin:
            nc.append("the config pin covers boots of the artifact with its golden config (conformance/golden); "
                      "configs that individual oracles write are not pinned")
        else:
            nc.append("config pin: not checked by this gate (no --config-pin)")
    nc += ["proofs and differential tests cover models, not the Rust code, unless a gate log says otherwise",
           "hyper, h2, tokio, rustls, the AWS-LC C code and rustc are trusted, not verified",
           "signatures are made with per-run throwaway test keys (D-P2); not a release attestation"]
    if profile == "floor":
        nc.append("FIPS approved mode: only the cmvp subject on AL2023 makes that claim")
    return nc


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- toml / gate specs


def load_gates(toml_path):
    spec = tomllib.load(open(toml_path, "rb"))
    gates, order = {}, []
    for g in spec["gate"]:
        gates[g["name"]] = g
        order.append(g["name"])
    return gates, order


def phase_of(toml_path):
    m = re.fullmatch(r"phase-(\d+)\.toml", os.path.basename(toml_path))
    return int(m[1]) if m else None


def marker_phase(lines):
    """The N of the marker's `phase=N` line (digits only), or None."""
    for l in lines:
        if l.startswith("phase=") and re.fullmatch(r"[0-9]+", l[6:].strip()):
            return int(l[6:].strip())
    return None


def read_marker(logdir):
    rs = os.path.join(logdir, ".run-start")
    return open(rs).read().splitlines() if os.path.isfile(rs) else None


def default_toml(logdir=None):
    """The marker's phase (a run judges its own phase), else the highest-numbered gates/phase-N.toml."""
    d = os.path.join(ROOT, "gates")
    marker = read_marker(logdir) if logdir else None
    ph = marker_phase(marker) if marker else None
    if ph is not None and os.path.isfile(os.path.join(d, f"phase-{ph}.toml")):
        return os.path.join(d, f"phase-{ph}.toml")
    ns = [int(m[1]) for f in os.listdir(d) if (m := re.fullmatch(r"phase-(\d+)\.toml", f))]
    return os.path.join(d, f"phase-{max(ns)}.toml") if ns else os.path.join(d, "phase-6.toml")


def invocation_args(cmd):
    """The argument list of a plain `[python3 -I] conformance/run ...` command line, else None."""
    try:
        t = shlex.split(cmd)
    except ValueError:
        return None
    if t[:2] == ["python3", "-I"]:
        t = t[2:]
    if not t or t[0] != "conformance/run" or any(x in ("&&", "||", ";", "|", "&") for x in t):
        return None
    return t[1:]


def find_self_gate(gates, order, step, argv):
    hits = [n for n in order if step in gates[n] and invocation_args(gates[n][step]) == list(argv)]
    return hits[0] if len(hits) == 1 else None


def gate_of(member):
    return EMBEDDED[member][0] if member in EMBEDDED else member


def check_map(gates, order, mode, trace_gates=()):
    """Members of required levels, digest gates and TRACE gates must be real gates placed before this gate; every
    level member must at least be a real gate. Returns a list of problems."""
    if mode.self_gate not in gates:
        return [f"this gate `{mode.self_gate}` is not a gate in the toml"]
    limit = order.index(mode.self_gate)
    must, known = set(DIGEST_GATES), set()
    for _, _, prof in SUBJECTS + [("fork", "fork", "cmvp")]:
        for L, members in levels_for(prof).items():
            for m in members or []:
                known.add(gate_of(m))
                if L in mode.required:
                    must.add(gate_of(m))
    if "C4" in mode.required:
        must |= {gate_of(m) for m in trace_gates}
    bad = []
    for n in sorted(must | known):
        if n not in gates:
            bad.append(f"{n}: not a gate in the toml")
        elif n in must and order.index(n) >= limit:
            bad.append(f"{n}: runs at or after {mode.self_gate}, so its log can never be from this run")
    return bad


def logged_cmds(g, step):
    cmd = g[step]
    out = [cmd]
    if g.get("remote"):
        host = g["remote"] if isinstance(g["remote"], str) else None
        out.append("ci/remote.sh " + (f"--host {shlex.quote(host)} " if host else "") + "bash -c " + shlex.quote(cmd))
    return out


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- log judgement


class Logs:
    def __init__(self, logdir, gates, order, phase, self_gate):
        self.dir, self.gates, self.order, self.phase, self.cache = logdir, gates, order, phase, {}
        self.limit = order.index(self_gate) if self_gate in order else len(order)
        rs = os.path.join(logdir, ".run-start")
        self.run_start = os.stat(rs).st_mtime_ns if os.path.isfile(rs) else None
        marker = open(rs).read().splitlines() if self.run_start is not None else []
        self.head = marker[0].strip() if marker else ""
        self.marker_phase = marker_phase(marker)

    def before(self, name):
        return name in self.gates and self.order.index(name) < self.limit

    def step(self, name, step):
        """(ok, sha256, reason, text) for one log."""
        key = (name, step)
        if key in self.cache:
            return self.cache[key]
        p = os.path.join(self.dir, f"phase{self.phase}-{name}-{step}.log")
        r = self._judge(name, step, p)
        self.cache[key] = r
        return r

    def _judge(self, name, step, p):
        if name not in self.gates:
            return False, EMPTY_SHA, f"{name} is not a gate in the toml", ""
        if self.run_start is None:
            return False, EMPTY_SHA, f"{step} log not judged: no .run-start in the log dir", ""
        if self.marker_phase is None:
            return False, EMPTY_SHA, f"{step} log not judged: .run-start has no phase=N line", ""
        if self.marker_phase != self.phase:
            return False, EMPTY_SHA, (f"{step} log not judged: .run-start is a phase={self.marker_phase} run, "
                                      f"the toml is phase {self.phase}"), ""
        if not self.before(name):
            return False, EMPTY_SHA, f"{name} runs after this gate, so its {step} log cannot be from this run", ""
        if os.path.islink(p) or (os.path.exists(p) and not os.path.isfile(p)):
            return False, EMPTY_SHA, f"{step} log is not a regular file", ""
        if not os.path.exists(p):
            return False, EMPTY_SHA, f"{step} log missing ({os.path.basename(p)})", ""
        data = open(p, "rb").read()
        h = hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()
        if os.stat(p).st_mtime_ns <= self.run_start:
            return False, h, f"{step} log stale (not newer than .run-start)", ""
        text = data.decode("utf-8", "replace")
        if not any(text.startswith(f"$ {c}\n") for c in logged_cmds(self.gates[name], step)):
            return False, h, f"{step} log does not start with this gate's command from the toml", text
        lines = [l for l in text.splitlines() if l.strip()]
        last = lines[-1] if lines else ""
        if last != "[exit 0]":
            return False, h, f"{step} log ends {last[:40]!r}, not [exit 0]", text
        return True, h, f"{step} log fresh, [exit 0]", text

    def gate(self, member):
        """(passed, log_sha256, reason) for a level member."""
        key = ("member", member)
        if key in self.cache:
            return self.cache[key]
        name, pats = (EMBEDDED[member][0], EMBEDDED[member][1:]) if member in EMBEDDED else (member, None)
        ok, h, why, text = self.step(name, "cmd")
        reasons = [why]
        if ok and pats and not re.search(pats[0], text, re.M):
            ok = False
            reasons.append(f"cmd log lacks a line matching {pats[0]}")
        if name in self.gates and "selftest" in self.gates[name]:
            sok, sh, swhy, stext = self.step(name, "selftest")
            reasons.append(swhy + ("" if sh == EMPTY_SHA and not sok else f" (selftest log sha256 {sh})"))
            if sok and pats and not re.search(pats[1], stext, re.M):
                sok = False
                reasons.append(f"selftest log lacks a line matching {pats[1]}")
            ok = ok and sok
        if ok and member in DRT:
            dok, dwhy = drt_verdict(member, text)
            ok = dok
            reasons.append(dwhy)
        r = (ok, h, "; ".join(reasons))
        self.cache[key] = r
        return r


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- C3: DRT verdict lines


def f8_profile_count():
    try:
        return len(json.load(open(F8))["$defs"]["listener"]["properties"]["profile"]["enum"])
    except (OSError, KeyError, ValueError, TypeError):
        return None


def _counters(body, keys):
    body = body.split(" engine_pin=[", 1)[0]
    seen = {}
    for tok in body.split():
        m = re.fullmatch(r"([A-Za-z0-9_]+)=(\d+)[;,)]*", tok)
        if m:
            seen.setdefault(m[1], []).append(int(m[2]))
    missing = [k for k in keys if k not in seen]
    return seen, missing


def _select(body):
    m = re.match(r"(\d+) profiles x (\d+) cases = (\d+), seed \S+, (\d+) divergence;", body)
    if not m:
        return False, "verdict body not `P profiles x n cases = N, seed s, D divergence;`"
    p, n, d = int(m[1]), int(m[3]), int(m[4])
    want = f8_profile_count()
    if want is None or p != want:
        return False, f"{p} profiles, want the {want} F8 profiles"
    if n <= 0 or d != 0:
        return False, f"{n} cases, {d} divergence"
    return True, f"{n} cases, 0 divergence"


def _token(body):
    m = re.match(r"(\d+) cases, (\d+) divergences\b", body)
    if not m:
        return False, "verdict body not `N cases, D divergences`"
    n, d = int(m[1]), int(m[2])
    return (n > 0 and d == 0), f"{n} cases, {d} divergences"


def _pdp(body):
    m = re.match(r"(\d+) cases match Cedar, (\d+) faulted exchanges all ERROR->DENY\b", body)
    if not m:
        return False, "verdict body not `N cases match Cedar, F faulted exchanges all ERROR->DENY`"
    n, f = int(m[1]), int(m[2])
    return (n > 0 and f > 0), f"{n} cases match, {f} faulted exchanges ERROR->DENY, 0 violations"


def _counted(keys):
    def parse(body):
        seen, missing = _counters(body, ("cases",) + keys)
        if missing:
            return False, f"verdict line lacks counter(s) {', '.join(missing)}"
        nz = {k: v for k in keys for v in seen[k] if v}
        if nz or min(seen["cases"]) <= 0:
            return False, f"cases={seen['cases'][0]} divergence " + (" ".join(f"{k}={v}" for k, v in nz.items()) or "-")
        return True, f"cases={seen['cases'][0]}, " + "=".join(("/".join(keys), "0"))
    return parse


_READ = _counted(("leak", "widen", "miss", "errors", "unrefused"))
_WRITE = _counted(("W1", "W2", "W4", "W6", "W7", "E", "FORM", "REFUSE", "BIND", "ACL"))
DRT = {"select-drt": ("SELECT-DRT", None, _select), TOKEN: ("TOKEN-DRT", "token-drt", _token),
       PDP: ("PDP-DST", "pdp-dst", _pdp)}
DRT.update({g: ("LOWERING-READ", None, _READ) for g in LOWER_READ})
DRT.update({g: ("LOWERING-WRITE", None, _WRITE) for g in LOWER_WRITE})


def drt_verdict(member, text):
    """(ok, reason): every verdict line of the member's oracle in its cmd log is PASS with 0 divergence."""
    name, tag, parse = DRT[member]
    pre = rf"\[{re.escape(tag)}\] " if tag else ""
    lines = re.findall(rf"^{pre}{re.escape(name)}: (PASS|FAIL) \((.*)\)\s*$", text, re.M)
    if not lines:
        return False, f"C3: no `{name}: PASS|FAIL (...)` verdict line in the cmd log"
    if member == "select-drt" and re.search(r"^DIVERGE ", text, re.M):
        return False, "C3: DIVERGE line in the cmd log"
    whys = []
    for verdict, body in lines:
        if verdict != "PASS":
            return False, f"C3: {name}: FAIL ({body[:80]})"
        ok, why = parse(body)
        if not ok:
            return False, f"C3: {name}: {why}"
        whys.append(why)
    return True, f"C3: {len(lines)} verdict line(s) at 0 divergence ({whys[0]})"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- C4: TRACE


class Trace:
    def __init__(self, path, gates, order, self_gate):
        self.path, self.problems, self.rows, self.ids, self.sha = path, [], {}, [], EMPTY_SHA
        try:
            raw = open(path, "rb").read()
            self.sha = hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()
            doc = tomllib.loads(raw.decode("utf-8"))
        except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError, tomllib.TOMLDecodeError) as e:
            self.problems.append(f"TRACE unreadable: {e}")
            return
        if doc.get("v") != 1:
            self.problems.append("TRACE v != 1")
        led = doc.get("ledger")
        if led != LEDGER_REL:
            self.problems.append(f"TRACE ledger {led!r} != {LEDGER_REL!r}")
            return
        lp = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path))), led)
        try:
            lraw = open(lp, "rb").read()
        except OSError as e:
            self.problems.append(f"ledger unreadable: {e}")
            return
        lsha = hashlib.sha256(lraw).hexdigest()
        if doc.get("ledger_sha256") != lsha:
            self.problems.append(f"TRACE ledger_sha256 {str(doc.get('ledger_sha256'))[:16]} != sha256 of {led} "
                                 f"{lsha[:16]} (re-frozen ledger: review the map)")
        for line in lraw.decode("utf-8", "replace").splitlines():
            f = line.split()
            if len(f) == 3:
                self.ids.append(f[2])
            elif line.strip():
                self.problems.append(f"ledger line not `hash kind id`: {line[:60]!r}")
        if not self.ids:
            self.problems.append("ledger has no statement ids")
        t = doc.get("trace")
        if not isinstance(t, dict):
            self.problems.append("TRACE has no [trace] table")
            return
        idset = set(self.ids)
        limit = order.index(self_gate) if self_gate in order else len(order)
        for sid, gl in t.items():
            if sid not in idset:
                self.problems.append(f"row {sid}: not a statement id of {led}")
                continue
            if not isinstance(gl, list) or not gl or not all(isinstance(x, str) for x in gl):
                self.problems.append(f"row {sid}: gates must be a non-empty list of strings")
                continue
            okrow = True
            for m in gl:
                g = gate_of(m)
                if "[" in m and m not in EMBEDDED:
                    self.problems.append(f"row {sid}: {m} is not an embedded member this runner knows")
                    okrow = False
                elif g not in gates:
                    self.problems.append(f"row {sid}: {m} is not a gate in the toml")
                    okrow = False
                elif order.index(g) >= limit:
                    self.problems.append(f"row {sid}: {m} runs at or after {self_gate}")
                    okrow = False
            if okrow:
                self.rows[sid] = list(dict.fromkeys(gl))

    def members(self):
        return list(dict.fromkeys(m for gl in self.rows.values() for m in gl))


def c4_entries(logs, trace):
    """(passed, total, entries, lines)."""
    entries, lines = [], []
    res = {m: logs.gate(m) for m in trace.members()}
    passed = 0
    for sid in trace.ids:
        row = trace.rows.get(sid)
        if row is None:
            entries.append({"name": sid, "result": "fail", "log_sha256": EMPTY_SHA,
                            "reason": "C4; F1 statement with no valid TRACE row"})
            lines.append(f"FAIL C4 {sid}: no valid TRACE row")
        elif all(res[m][0] for m in row):
            passed += 1
        else:
            bad = [m for m in row if not res[m][0]]
            entries.append({"name": sid, "result": "fail", "log_sha256": EMPTY_SHA,
                            "reason": f"C4; F1 statement whose mapped gate(s) failed: {', '.join(bad)}"})
            lines.append(f"FAIL C4 {sid}: mapped gate(s) failed: {', '.join(bad)}")
    count = {}
    for row in trace.rows.values():
        for m in row:
            count[m] = count.get(m, 0) + 1
    for m in trace.members():
        ok, h, why = res[m]
        entries.append({"name": m, "result": "pass" if ok else "fail", "log_sha256": h,
                        "reason": f"C4; evidence for {count[m]} F1 statement(s); {why}"})
        lines.append(f"{'pass' if ok else 'FAIL'} C4 {m:30s} ({count[m]} statements) {why}")
    tok = not trace.problems
    passed += tok
    probs = sorted(trace.problems, key=lambda p: "runs at or after" in p)  # the specific ones first
    entries.append({"name": TRACE_MEMBER, "result": "pass" if tok else "fail", "log_sha256": trace.sha,
                    "reason": f"C4; TRACE file (log_sha256 = sha256 of spec/TRACE.toml); {len(trace.rows)}/"
                              f"{len(trace.ids)} ledger ids mapped"
                              + ("" if tok else f"; {len(probs)} problem(s): " + "; ".join(probs[:5]))})
    lines.append(f"{'pass' if tok else 'FAIL'} C4 {TRACE_MEMBER:30s} {len(trace.rows)}/{len(trace.ids)} ids mapped"
                 + ("" if tok else f"; {len(probs)} problem(s): " + "; ".join(probs[:5])))
    return passed, len(trace.ids) + 1, entries, lines


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- config pin


BOOT_RE = re.compile(r"^CONFORMANCE-BOOT: ([A-Za-z0-9._-]+) artifact ([0-9a-f]{64}) config ([0-9a-f]{64})\b", re.M)


def load_pins(path):
    """{subject: config_sha256 or None}, problems."""
    try:
        doc = tomllib.load(open(path, "rb"))
    except (OSError, tomllib.TOMLDecodeError) as e:
        return {}, [f"config pins unreadable: {e}"]
    out, bad = {}, []
    if doc.get("v") != 1:
        bad.append("config-pin.toml v != 1")
    for name, ent in (doc.get("subject") or {}).items():
        h = ent.get("config_sha256") if isinstance(ent, dict) else None
        out[name] = h if isinstance(h, str) and HEX64.search(h) and "\n" not in h else None
    return out, bad


def boot_records(logs):
    """{subject: [(gate, artifact, config, log_sha256)]} from passing cmd logs of gates before this gate."""
    recs = {}
    for g in logs.order[:logs.limit]:
        ok, h, _, text = logs.step(g, "cmd")
        if not ok:
            continue
        for m in BOOT_RE.finditer(text):
            recs.setdefault(m[1], []).append((g, m[2], m[3], h))
    return recs


def config_pin(name, digest, pins, pin_problems, recs):
    """(ok, entry, line)."""
    pin = pins.get(name)
    rs = recs.get(name, [])
    why = None
    if pin_problems:
        why = "; ".join(pin_problems)
    elif pin is None:
        why = f"no 64-hex config_sha256 pinned for {name} in conformance/config-pin.toml"
    elif not rs:
        why = "no CONFORMANCE-BOOT record for this subject in any passing cmd log of this run"
    else:
        for g, art, cfg, _ in rs:
            if cfg != pin:
                why = f"subject booted with effective-config hash {cfg[:16]} in {g}; the pin is {pin[:16]}"
                break
            if art != digest:
                why = f"booted artifact {art[:16]} in {g} is not the judged artifact {(digest or '-')[:16]}"
                break
    ok = why is None
    if ok:
        why = f"booted with the pinned effective-config hash {pin} in " + ",".join(sorted({g for g, *_ in rs}))
    entry = {"name": CONFIG_PIN_MEMBER, "result": "pass" if ok else "fail",
             "log_sha256": rs[0][3] if rs else EMPTY_SHA, "reason": f"config pin; {why}"}
    return ok, entry, f"  {'pass' if ok else 'FAIL'} {name:16s} config-pin {why}"


PIPE_RE = re.compile(r"RELEASE-PIPELINE: PASS \((floor|cmvp), artifacts/monban-(floor|cmvp) sha256 ([0-9a-f]{64})\b")
ART_RE = re.compile(r"CONFORMANCE-ARTIFACT: ([A-Za-z0-9._-]+) sha256 ([0-9a-f]{64})\b")


def artifact_digest(logs, subject, profile, member_gates):
    found = {}
    for g in DIGEST_GATES + [m for m in member_gates if m in logs.gates]:
        ok, _, _, text = logs.step(g, "cmd")
        if not ok:
            continue
        for m in PIPE_RE.finditer(text):
            if m[1] == m[2] == profile:
                found.setdefault(m[3], set()).add(g)
        for m in ART_RE.finditer(text):
            if m[1] == subject:
                found.setdefault(m[2], set()).add(g)
    if not found:
        return None, "no artifact digest in any passing log of this run (RELEASE-PIPELINE / CONFORMANCE-ARTIFACT)"
    if len(found) > 1:
        return None, "conflicting artifact digests: " + ", ".join(f"{d[:12]} in {sorted(s)}" for d, s in found.items())
    d, src = next(iter(found.items()))
    return d, "from " + ",".join(sorted(src))


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- report


def canonical(report):
    body = {k: v for k, v in report.items() if k != "signatures"}
    return json.dumps(body, sort_keys=True, separators=(",", ":"), ensure_ascii=False).encode("utf-8")


def toolchain():
    try:
        ch = tomllib.load(open(os.path.join(ROOT, "rust-toolchain.toml"), "rb"))["toolchain"]["channel"]
    except (OSError, KeyError, tomllib.TOMLDecodeError):
        ch = "unknown"
    return f"rust {ch} (rust-toolchain.toml)"


def ws_version():
    try:
        return tomllib.load(open(os.path.join(ROOT, "Cargo.toml"), "rb"))["workspace"]["package"]["version"]
    except (OSError, KeyError, tomllib.TOMLDecodeError):
        return "0.0.0"


def build_report(logs, name, kind, profile, now, mode, ctx):
    """Returns (report or None, gated_ok, lines)."""
    lv = levels_for(profile)
    lines, gates_out, levels = [], [], {}
    gated_ok = True
    gated = mode.gated(profile)
    for L in LEVELS:
        if L not in lv:
            continue
        tag = "" if L in gated else " (reported, not gated)"
        if L == "C4":
            passed, total, ents, ls = c4_entries(logs, ctx["trace"])
            for e in ents:
                e["reason"] = e["reason"].replace("C4;", f"C4{tag};", 1)
            gates_out += ents
            lines += [f"  {l.split(' ', 1)[0]} {name:16s} {l.split(' ', 1)[1]}" for l in ls]
        else:
            passed, total = 0, len(lv[L])
            for m in lv[L]:
                ok, h, why = logs.gate(m)
                passed += ok
                gates_out.append({"name": m, "result": "pass" if ok else "fail", "log_sha256": h,
                                  "reason": f"{L}{tag}; {why}"})
                lines.append(f"  {'pass' if ok else 'FAIL'} {name:16s} {L} {m:30s} {why}")
        levels[L] = {"passed": passed, "total": total}
        if L in gated and passed != total:
            gated_ok = False
    members = [m for L, ms in lv.items() if ms for m in ms]
    digest, dwhy = artifact_digest(logs, name, profile, members)
    lines.append(f"  {'pass' if digest else 'FAIL'} {name:16s} artifact_sha256 {digest or '-'} {dwhy}")
    if not digest:
        return None, False, lines
    pin_ok, pin = True, None
    if mode.config_pin and kind != "module":
        pin_ok, entry, pl = config_pin(name, digest, ctx["pins"], ctx["pin_problems"], ctx["boots"])
        lines.append(pl)
        if not pin_ok:
            lines.append(f"  FAIL {name:16s} report refused: config pin failed")
            return None, False, lines
        gates_out.append(entry)
        pin = ctx["pins"][name]
    head = logs.head[:12] if re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{40}|[0-9a-f]{64}", logs.head) else ""
    report = {
        "v": 1,
        "subject": {"name": name, "version": ws_version() + (f"+g{head}" if head else ""), "kind": kind},
        "artifact_sha256": digest,
        "toolchain": toolchain() + (f"; profile {profile}" if profile != "module" else ""),
        "generated_at": now,
        "levels": levels,
        "gated": gated,
        "gates": gates_out,
        "not_claimed": not_claimed(profile, mode),
        "test_keys": True,
    }
    if pin:
        report["config_sha256"] = pin
    return report, gated_ok and pin_ok, lines


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- strict F13 validator


def strict_validate(r):
    """Exactly the frozen F13 schema. Returns a list of errors (empty = valid)."""
    e = []

    def isint(x):
        return isinstance(x, int) and not isinstance(x, bool)

    def hex64(x):
        return isinstance(x, str) and HEX64.search(x) is not None and "\n" not in x

    if not isinstance(r, dict):
        return ["report is not an object"]
    allowed = {"v", "subject", "artifact_sha256", "toolchain", "generated_at", "levels", "gates", "not_claimed",
               "test_keys", "signatures", "config_sha256", "gated"}
    for k in r:
        if k not in allowed:
            e.append(f"unknown member {k}")
    for k in ("v", "subject", "artifact_sha256", "toolchain", "generated_at", "levels", "gates", "signatures"):
        if k not in r:
            e.append(f"missing {k}")
    if "v" in r and not (isint(r["v"]) and r["v"] == 1) and not (isinstance(r["v"], float) and r["v"] == 1.0):
        e.append("v != 1")
    s = r.get("subject")
    if "subject" in r:
        if not isinstance(s, dict):
            e.append("subject not an object")
        else:
            for k in s:
                if k not in ("name", "version", "kind"):
                    e.append(f"subject: unknown member {k}")
            for k in ("name", "version", "kind"):
                if k not in s:
                    e.append(f"subject: missing {k}")
            for k in ("name", "version"):
                if k in s and not isinstance(s[k], str):
                    e.append(f"subject.{k} not a string")
            if "kind" in s and s["kind"] not in ("golden", "adapter", "module", "fork"):
                e.append("subject.kind not in enum")
    if "artifact_sha256" in r and not hex64(r["artifact_sha256"]):
        e.append("artifact_sha256 not 64 lowercase hex")
    if "config_sha256" in r and not hex64(r["config_sha256"]):
        e.append("config_sha256 not 64 lowercase hex")
    if "gated" in r:
        g = r["gated"]
        if not (isinstance(g, list) and all(isinstance(x, str) and x in LEVELS for x in g) and len(set(g)) == len(g)):
            e.append("gated not an array of unique level names C0-C4")
    if "toolchain" in r and not isinstance(r["toolchain"], str):
        e.append("toolchain not a string")
    if "generated_at" in r:
        g = r["generated_at"]
        if not isinstance(g, str) or not re.fullmatch(
                r"\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}[Tt]\d{2}:\d{2}:\d{2}(\.\d+)?([Zz]|[+-]\d{2}:\d{2})", g):
            e.append("generated_at not an RFC 3339 date-time")
        else:
            try:
                datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(g.replace("Z", "+00:00").replace("z", "+00:00"))
            except ValueError:
                e.append("generated_at not a valid date-time")
    if "levels" in r:
        lv = r["levels"]
        if not isinstance(lv, dict):
            e.append("levels not an object")
        else:
            for k, v in lv.items():
                if not re.search(r"^C[0-4]$", k) or "\n" in k:
                    e.append(f"levels: member {k} not allowed")
                    continue
                if not isinstance(v, dict):
                    e.append(f"levels.{k} not an object")
                    continue
                for f in ("passed", "total"):
                    if f not in v:
                        e.append(f"levels.{k}: missing {f}")
                    elif not (isint(v[f]) or (isinstance(v[f], float) and v[f].is_integer())) or v[f] < 0:
                        e.append(f"levels.{k}.{f} not a non-negative integer")
    if "gates" in r:
        gs = r["gates"]
        if not isinstance(gs, list):
            e.append("gates not an array")
        else:
            for i, g in enumerate(gs):
                if not isinstance(g, dict):
                    e.append(f"gates[{i}] not an object")
                    continue
                for k in g:
                    if k not in ("name", "result", "reason", "log_sha256"):
                        e.append(f"gates[{i}]: unknown member {k}")
                for k in ("name", "result", "log_sha256"):
                    if k not in g:
                        e.append(f"gates[{i}]: missing {k}")
                for k in ("name", "reason"):
                    if k in g and not isinstance(g[k], str):
                        e.append(f"gates[{i}].{k} not a string")
                if "result" in g and g["result"] not in ("pass", "fail", "skipped"):
                    e.append(f"gates[{i}].result not in enum")
                if "log_sha256" in g and not hex64(g["log_sha256"]):
                    e.append(f"gates[{i}].log_sha256 not 64 lowercase hex")
    if "not_claimed" in r and not (isinstance(r["not_claimed"], list)
                                   and all(isinstance(x, str) for x in r["not_claimed"])):
        e.append("not_claimed not an array of strings")
    if "test_keys" in r and not isinstance(r["test_keys"], bool):
        e.append("test_keys not a boolean")
    if "signatures" in r:
        sg = r["signatures"]
        if not isinstance(sg, list) or len(sg) != 3:
            e.append("signatures not an array of exactly 3")
        else:
            for i, (x, alg) in enumerate(zip(sg, ALGS)):
                if not isinstance(x, dict):
                    e.append(f"signatures[{i}] not an object")
                    continue
                for k in x:
                    if k not in ("alg", "sig"):
                        e.append(f"signatures[{i}]: unknown member {k}")
                if x.get("alg") != alg:
                    e.append(f"signatures[{i}].alg must be {alg}")
                if not (isinstance(x.get("sig"), str) and re.search(r"^[A-Za-z0-9+/]+={0,2}$", x["sig"])
                        and "\n" not in x["sig"]):
                    e.append(f"signatures[{i}].sig not standard base64")
    return e


def jsonschema_validate(r):
    """Returns (ran, errors)."""
    try:
        import jsonschema
    except ImportError:
        return False, []
    schema = json.load(open(SCHEMA))
    v = jsonschema.Draft202012Validator(schema, format_checker=jsonschema.Draft202012Validator.FORMAT_CHECKER)
    return True, [f"{'/'.join(map(str, x.absolute_path))}: {x.message}" for x in v.iter_errors(r)]


def jsonschema_checks_datetime():
    try:
        import jsonschema
    except ImportError:
        return False
    return "date-time" in jsonschema.Draft202012Validator.FORMAT_CHECKER.checkers


def validate(r):
    errs = strict_validate(r)
    ran, jerrs = jsonschema_validate(r)
    return errs + [f"jsonschema: {x}" for x in jerrs], ran




# ---------------------------------------------------------------- OpenSSL signer (remote)

SIGN_SH = r"""
set -euo pipefail
umask 077
O=/usr/bin/openssl
v=$($O version); case "$v" in "OpenSSL 3."[5-9]*|"OpenSSL 3."[1-9][0-9]*|"OpenSSL "[4-9]*) ;; *) echo "ERR openssl $v"; exit 1;; esac
d=$(mktemp -d)
trap 'rm -rf "$d"' EXIT
for a in ed25519:ED25519 slh-dsa-sha2-128s:SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s ml-dsa-87:ML-DSA-87; do
  n=${a%%:*}
  $O genpkey -algorithm "${a#*:}" -out "$d/$n.key" 2>/dev/null
  echo "PUB $n $($O pkey -in "$d/$n.key" -pubout | base64 -w0)"
done
i=0
while IFS= read -r line; do
  printf '%s' "$line" | base64 -d > "$d/m"
  for n in ed25519 slh-dsa-sha2-128s ml-dsa-87; do
    echo "SIG $i $n $($O pkeyutl -sign -rawin -inkey "$d/$n.key" -in "$d/m" | base64 -w0)"
  done
  i=$((i+1))
done
rm -rf "$d"
[ ! -e "$d" ] && echo "DESTROYED $i"
"""

VERIFY_SH = r"""
set -euo pipefail
umask 077
O=/usr/bin/openssl
d=$(mktemp -d)
trap 'rm -rf "$d"' EXIT
while IFS=' ' read -r t a b c; do
  case "$t" in
    PUB) printf '%s' "$b" | base64 -d > "$d/$a.pub"
         echo "TYPE $a $($O pkey -pubin -in "$d/$a.pub" -noout -text 2>/dev/null | head -1 | tr -d '\r')" ;;
    V) printf '%s' "$b" | base64 -d > "$d/m"; printf '%s' "$c" | base64 -d > "$d/s"
       if $O pkeyutl -verify -rawin -pubin -inkey "$d/${a#*/}.pub" -in "$d/m" -sigfile "$d/s" 2>/dev/null \
            | grep -q 'Signature Verified Successfully'; then echo "R $a OK"; else echo "R $a BAD"; fi ;;
  esac
done
echo END
"""


class Signer:
    def __init__(self, host=None):
        self.host = host or os.environ.get("AEGIS_CONFORMANCE_SIGN_HOST", "kamrui")

    def _run(self, script, stdin):
        if self.host == "local":
            argv = ["bash", "-c", script]
        else:
            argv = ["ssh", "-o", "BatchMode=yes", "-o", "ConnectTimeout=10", self.host, "bash -c " + shlex.quote(script)]
        p = subprocess.run(argv, input=stdin, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=600)
        if p.returncode != 0:
            raise RuntimeError(f"signing host {self.host}: exit {p.returncode}: {(p.stdout + p.stderr).strip()[-300:]}")
        return p.stdout.splitlines()

    def sign(self, messages):
        """messages: list of bytes -> (pubs {alg: pem bytes}, sigs [ {alg: raw bytes} ])."""
        out = self._run(SIGN_SH, "".join(base64.b64encode(m).decode() + "\n" for m in messages))
        pubs, sigs, destroyed = {}, [dict() for _ in messages], False
        for line in out:
            f = line.split(" ")
            if f[0] == "PUB" and len(f) == 3:
                pubs[f[1]] = base64.b64decode(f[2], validate=True)
            elif f[0] == "SIG" and len(f) == 4:
                sigs[int(f[1])][f[2]] = base64.b64decode(f[3], validate=True)
            elif f[0] == "DESTROYED" and f[1:] == [str(len(messages))]:
                destroyed = True
        if not destroyed:
            raise RuntimeError("signing host did not confirm the key dir was destroyed")
        for a in ALGS:
            if a not in pubs or b"PRIVATE KEY" in pubs[a] or b"PUBLIC KEY" not in pubs[a]:
                raise RuntimeError(f"no valid public key for {a}")
        for s in sigs:
            for a in ALGS:
                if len(s.get(a, b"")) != SIG_LEN[a]:
                    raise RuntimeError(f"{a} signature has length {len(s.get(a, b''))}, want {SIG_LEN[a]}")
        return pubs, sigs

    def verify(self, pubs, items):
        """items: list of (message bytes, {alg: raw sig}) -> list of per-item {alg: bool}; key types are checked."""
        lines = []
        for a in ALGS:
            if b"PRIVATE KEY" in pubs[a]:
                raise RuntimeError("private key material offered for verification")
            lines.append(f"PUB {a} {base64.b64encode(pubs[a]).decode()}")
        for i, (msg, sg) in enumerate(items):
            for a in ALGS:
                lines.append(f"V {i}/{a} {base64.b64encode(msg).decode()} "
                             f"{base64.b64encode(sg.get(a, b'')).decode() or 'AA=='}")
        out = self._run(VERIFY_SH, "".join(l + "\n" for l in lines))
        if not out or out[-1] != "END":
            raise RuntimeError("verification session did not complete")
        types = {l.split(" ", 2)[1]: l.split(" ", 2)[2] if len(l.split(" ", 2)) > 2 else ""
                 for l in out if l.startswith("TYPE ")}
        typeok = all(OSSL_ALG[a] in types.get(a, "") for a in ALGS)
        res = [{a: False for a in ALGS} for _ in items]
        for l in out:
            f = l.split(" ")
            if f[0] == "R" and len(f) == 3:
                i, a = f[1].split("/", 1)
                res[int(i)][a] = typeok and f[2] == "OK"
        return res


def sigs_from_report(r):
    out = {}
    for x in r.get("signatures", []) if isinstance(r.get("signatures"), list) else []:
        if isinstance(x, dict) and x.get("alg") in ALGS and isinstance(x.get("sig"), str):
            try:
                out[x["alg"]] = base64.b64decode(x["sig"], validate=True)
            except (binascii.Error, ValueError):
                pass
    # the fixed order is a schema rule; positional mismatch is caught by validate()
    return out


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- run


def now_utc():
    return datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).replace(microsecond=0).isoformat().replace("+00:00", "Z")


def evaluate(logdir, outdir, toml_path, subjects, signer, gated_names, mode):
    """Writes reports, verifies them back. Returns (ok, lines, {name: report-or-None}, pubs)."""
    gates, order = load_gates(toml_path)
    phase = phase_of(toml_path)
    lines = []
    trace = Trace(mode.trace, gates, order, mode.self_gate)
    problems = check_map(gates, order, mode, trace.members())
    if phase is None:
        problems.append(f"{toml_path}: not a gates/phase-N.toml")
    if "C4" in mode.required and trace.problems:
        # an invalid map is judged (C4 red), but a map naming gates after this one is a map error, like the level map
        problems += [p for p in trace.problems if "runs at or after" in p]
    if problems:
        return False, [f"level map: {p}" for p in problems], {}, None
    logs = Logs(logdir, gates, order, phase, mode.self_gate)
    if logs.run_start is None:
        lines.append(f"  FAIL no {os.path.join(logdir, '.run-start')}: every log counts as fail")
    pins, pin_problems = load_pins(mode.pins) if mode.config_pin else ({}, [])
    ctx = {"trace": trace, "pins": pins, "pin_problems": pin_problems,
           "boots": boot_records(logs) if mode.config_pin else {}}
    os.makedirs(outdir, exist_ok=True)
    now = now_utc()
    reports, ok = {}, True
    for name, kind, profile in subjects:
        rep, gated_ok, ls = build_report(logs, name, kind, profile, now, mode, ctx)
        lines += ls
        p = os.path.join(outdir, f"{name}.json")
        if rep is None:
            if os.path.lexists(p):
                os.remove(p)  # never leave an earlier run's report standing for this subject
            ok = False
        if name in gated_names and not gated_ok:
            ok = False
        reports[name] = rep
        if rep is not None:
            summ = " ".join(f"{L} {v['passed']}/{v['total']}" for L, v in rep["levels"].items())
            pin = f" config {rep['config_sha256'][:12]}" if "config_sha256" in rep else ""
            lines.append(f"SUBJECT {name}: {summ}{pin}"
                         f"{'' if gated_ok else ' (required levels ' + ','.join(rep['gated']) + ' not 100%)'}")
        else:
            lines.append(f"SUBJECT {name}: no report (no artifact digest, or config pin refused)")
    todo = [n for n in reports if reports[n] is not None]
    pubs = None
    if todo:
        pubs, sigs = signer.sign([canonical(reports[n]) for n in todo])
        kd = os.path.join(outdir, "keys")
        os.makedirs(kd, exist_ok=True)
        for a in ALGS:
            with open(os.path.join(kd, f"{a}.pub.pem"), "wb") as f:
                f.write(pubs[a])
        for n, sg in zip(todo, sigs):
            reports[n]["signatures"] = [{"alg": a, "sig": base64.b64encode(sg[a]).decode()} for a in ALGS]
            with open(os.path.join(outdir, f"{n}.json"), "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
                json.dump(reports[n], f, indent=1, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)
                f.write("\n")
        vok, vlines = verify_reports(outdir, todo, pubs, signer)
        lines += vlines
        ok = ok and vok
    return ok, lines, reports, pubs


def verify_reports(outdir, names, pubs, signer):
    """Re-reads each report from disk: schema + all three signatures over its canonical bytes."""
    ok, lines, items, loaded = True, [], [], []
    for n in names:
        p = os.path.join(outdir, f"{n}.json")
        try:
            r = json.load(open(p, encoding="utf-8"))
        except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
            lines.append(f"  FAIL {n}: report unreadable: {e}")
            ok = False
            continue
        errs, ran = validate(r)
        if errs:
            lines.append(f"  FAIL {n}: F13 schema: {'; '.join(errs[:5])}")
            ok = False
        else:
            lines.append(f"  pass {n}: F13 schema (strict validator{' + jsonschema 2020-12' if ran else ''})")
        items.append((canonical(r) if isinstance(r, dict) else b"", sigs_from_report(r) if isinstance(r, dict) else {}))
        loaded.append(n)
    if items:
        res = signer.verify(pubs, items)
        for n, rv in zip(loaded, res):
            good = all(rv.values())
            ok = ok and good
            lines.append(f"  {'pass' if good else 'FAIL'} {n}: signatures "
                         + " ".join(f"{a}={'ok' if rv[a] else 'BAD'}" for a in ALGS))
    return ok, lines


def parse_required(s):
    if s is None:
        return LEGACY_REQUIRED
    req = tuple(x for x in s.split(",") if x)
    bad = [x for x in req if x not in LEVELS]
    if bad or not req or len(set(req)) != len(req):
        raise ValueError(f"--require {s!r}: want a comma list of distinct levels from {','.join(LEVELS)}")
    return tuple(L for L in LEVELS if L in req)


def resolve_mode(a, toml_path, step):
    """(Mode, None) or (None, error)."""
    required = parse_required(a.require)
    gates, order = load_gates(toml_path)
    me = a.gate or find_self_gate(gates, order, step, a.argv)
    if me is None and step == "selftest":
        me = "conformance-full" if (a.config_pin or set(required) - set(LEGACY_REQUIRED)) else "conformance"
    if me is None:
        return None, (f"this invocation ({' '.join(a.argv) or 'no args'}) is not the {step} of exactly one gate in "
                      f"{os.path.relpath(toml_path, ROOT)}; pass --gate NAME")
    if me not in gates:
        return None, f"--gate {me}: not a gate in {os.path.relpath(toml_path, ROOT)}"
    return Mode(required, a.config_pin, me), None


def main_run(a):
    logdir = a.logs if os.path.isabs(a.logs) else os.path.join(ROOT, a.logs)
    outdir = a.out if os.path.isabs(a.out) else os.path.join(ROOT, a.out)
    if a.toml is None:
        marker = read_marker(logdir)
        ph = marker_phase(marker) if marker else None
        if ph is None:
            print(f"CONFORMANCE: FAIL ({os.path.join(logdir, '.run-start')} missing or without a phase=N line; "
                  f"pass --toml to name the gate file)")
            return 1
        a.toml = f"gates/phase-{ph}.toml"
    toml_path = a.toml if os.path.isabs(a.toml) else os.path.join(ROOT, a.toml)
    try:
        mode, err = resolve_mode(a, toml_path, "cmd")
    except (ValueError, OSError, tomllib.TOMLDecodeError) as e:
        mode, err = None, str(e)
    if mode is None:
        print(f"CONFORMANCE: FAIL (usage: {err})")
        return 2
    for n in NOTES:
        print(f"note: {n}")
    print(f"note: this gate {mode.self_gate}; required {','.join(mode.required)}; config pin "
          f"{'on' if mode.config_pin else 'off'}; toml {os.path.relpath(toml_path, ROOT)}")
    try:
        ok, lines, reports, _ = evaluate(logdir, outdir, toml_path, SUBJECTS, Signer(), {n for n, _, _ in GOLDEN},
                                         mode)
    except (RuntimeError, OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        print(f"CONFORMANCE: FAIL ({e})")
        return 1
    for l in lines:
        print(l)
    summ = "; ".join(
        f"{n} " + (" ".join(f"{L} {v['passed']}/{v['total']}" for L, v in r["levels"].items())
                   + (f" config {r['config_sha256'][:12]}" if "config_sha256" in r else "") if r else "no report")
        for n, r in reports.items())
    print(f"CONFORMANCE: {'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL'} (required {','.join(mode.required)}"
          f"{' + config pin' if mode.config_pin else ''}; {summ or 'level map invalid'})")
    return 0 if ok else 1


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- self-test


def synth_pins(path, values):
    with open(path, "w") as f:
        f.write("v = 1\n")
        for n, h in values.items():
            f.write(f'\n[subject.{n}]\nconfig = "conformance/golden/x.f8.json"\nconfig_sha256 = "{h}"\n')


def write_synth(d, gates, phase, pins, mutate=None, marker_phase_line=None):
    """Synthetic all-pass log dir. mutate(name, step, content) -> content | None (None = omit the file)."""
    os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
    rs = os.path.join(d, ".run-start")
    with open(rs, "w") as f:
        f.write("0" * 40 + "\n" + (f"phase={phase}\n" if marker_phase_line is None else marker_phase_line))
    t0 = 1_800_000_000
    os.utime(rs, (t0, t0))
    floor, cmvp, p2 = (hashlib.sha256(x).hexdigest() for x in (b"floor", b"cmvp", b"p2"))
    np = f8_profile_count() or 8

    def boot(subj, art):
        return f"CONFORMANCE-BOOT: {subj} artifact {art} config {pins[subj]} (synthetic)\n" if subj in pins else ""
    extra = {
        "release-verify": f"RELEASE-PIPELINE: PASS (floor, artifacts/monban-floor sha256 {floor}, 9 files)\n"
                          + boot("monban-bin-floor", floor),
        "release-rebuild": f"[A] RELEASE-PIPELINE: PASS (floor, artifacts/monban-floor sha256 {floor}, 9 files)\n"
                           f"[A] RELEASE-PIPELINE: PASS (cmvp, artifacts/monban-cmvp sha256 {cmvp}, 9 files)\n"
                           + boot("monban-bin-cmvp", cmvp) + boot("fork-cmvp-tls-client", cmvp),
        "p2-hostile-host": f"CONFORMANCE-ARTIFACT: monban-p2 sha256 {p2}\n",
        "select-drt": f"PROFILE P-PUBLIC-WEB      cases=100000 sh=1 hrr=1 alert=1\nSELECT-DRT: PASS ({np} profiles x "
                      f"100000 cases = {np * 100000}, seed 1, 0 divergence; Lean table == F12; rung R4 model + R2)\n",
    }
    for g in LOWER_READ:
        extra[g] = ("LOWERING-READ: subject=x engines=['sqlite']\nLOWERING-READ: PASS (cases=12000 generated_unique["
                    "sqlite=9000 redis_model=0] (sqlite x3 schemas=4000; pg x4 schemas x0 engines) leak=0 widen=0 "
                    "miss=0 gap_vs_2vl(info)=12 errors=0 unrefused=0 engine_pin=[sqlite 3.50 -> OK])\n")
    for g in LOWER_WRITE:
        extra[g] = ("LOWERING-WRITE: PASS (cases=300 families=9 W1=0 W2=0 W4=0 W6=0 W7=0 E=0 FORM=0 REFUSE=0 BIND=0 "
                    "ACL=0 engine_pin=[x E=1 -> OK])\n")
    emb = {"oracles-remote": {"cmd": "[ssrf-corpus] SSRF-CORPUS: PASS (all cases)\n"
                                     "[pdp-dst] PDP-DST: PASS (40 cases match Cedar, 224 faulted exchanges all "
                                     "ERROR->DENY, 3 recoveries, 2 PDP kills, 3 invalid policy sets refused, stdio "
                                     "mode ok)\n",
                              "selftest": "[ssrf-corpus] SSRF-CORPUS SELF-TEST: PASS (reference passes)\n"
                                          "[pdp-dst] PDP-DST SELF-TEST: PASS (reference client passes)\n"},
           "oracles-local": {"cmd": "[token-drt] TOKEN-DRT: PASS (1000000 cases, 0 divergences)\n",
                             "selftest": "[token-drt] TOKEN-DRT SELF-TEST: PASS (9/9 mutants caught; baseline 0 "
                                         "divergences)\n"}}
    for name, g in gates.items():
        for step in ("cmd", "selftest"):
            if step not in g:
                continue
            body = f"synthetic output of {name} {step}\n" + (extra.get(name, "") if step == "cmd" else "")
            body += emb.get(name, {}).get(step, "")
            content = f"$ {g[step]}\n{body}\n[exit 0]\n"
            mtime = t0 + 10
            if mutate:
                r = mutate(name, step, content)
                if r is None:
                    continue
                content, mtime = r if isinstance(r, tuple) else (r, mtime)
            p = os.path.join(d, f"phase{phase}-{name}-{step}.log")
            with open(p, "w") as f:
                f.write(content)
            os.utime(p, (mtime, mtime))
    return {"floor": floor, "cmvp": cmvp, "p2": p2}


def self_test(a):
    toml_path = a.toml if os.path.isabs(a.toml) else os.path.join(ROOT, a.toml)
    try:
        mode, err = resolve_mode(a, toml_path, "selftest")
    except (ValueError, OSError, tomllib.TOMLDecodeError) as e:
        mode, err = None, str(e)
    if mode is None:
        print(f"CONFORMANCE SELF-TEST: FAIL (usage: {err})")
        return 2
    gates, order = load_gates(toml_path)
    phase = phase_of(toml_path)
    req = set(mode.required)
    print(f"  mode: this gate {mode.self_gate}; required {','.join(mode.required)}; config pin "
          f"{'on' if mode.config_pin else 'off'}; toml {os.path.relpath(toml_path, ROOT)}")
    signer = Signer()
    results, bad = [], []
    tmp = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="monban-conformance-st-")
    golden = {n for n, _, _ in GOLDEN}
    fork = ("fork-cmvp-tls-client", "fork", "cmvp")
    pin_vals = {n: hashlib.sha256(f"config of {n}".encode()).hexdigest() for n in golden | {fork[0]}}
    pin_path = os.path.join(tmp, "config-pin.toml")
    synth_pins(pin_path, pin_vals)

    def M(**kw):
        m = Mode(mode.required, mode.config_pin, mode.self_gate, pins=pin_path)
        for k, v in kw.items():
            setattr(m, k, v)
        return m

    def case(label, mutate, expect_ok, subjects=SUBJECTS, check=None, m=None, **synth):
        d = os.path.join(tmp, label, "logs")
        o = os.path.join(tmp, label, "out")
        write_synth(d, gates, phase, pin_vals, mutate, **synth)
        ok, lines, reports, pubs = evaluate(d, o, toml_path, subjects, signer, golden | {fork[0]}, m or M())
        extra_ok, why = (check(lines, reports, o, pubs) if check else (True, ""))
        good = (ok == expect_ok) and extra_ok
        results.append(label)
        print(f"  {'ok  ' if good else 'BAD '} {label}: run {'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL'} "
              f"(expected {'PASS' if expect_ok else 'FAIL'}){'; ' + why if why else ''}")
        if not good:
            bad.append(label)
            for l in lines:
                print("      " + l)
        return reports, o, pubs

    def entry(reports, subj, gate):
        r = reports.get(subj) or {}
        return next((g for g in r.get("gates", []) if g["name"] == gate), None)

    def expect_entry(subj, gate, needle, level=None, fails=1):
        def chk(lines, reports, o, pubs):
            e = entry(reports, subj, gate)
            if not e or e["result"] != "fail" or needle not in e.get("reason", ""):
                return False, f"{subj}/{gate} not failed with '{needle}': {e}"
            if level:
                lv = reports[subj]["levels"][level]
                if lv["passed"] > lv["total"] - fails:
                    return False, f"{subj} {level} {lv}, want >= {fails} fail"
            if any(g["result"] == "skipped" for r in reports.values() if r for g in r["gates"]):
                return False, "a result was 'skipped'"
            return True, f"{subj} {gate}: {e['reason'][:80]}"
        return chk

    def refused(subj, needle):
        def chk(lines, reports, o, pubs):
            gone = reports.get(subj) is None and not os.path.exists(os.path.join(o, f"{subj}.json"))
            hit = any(subj in l and needle in l for l in lines)
            return gone and hit, f"{subj}: report refused ({needle})" if gone and hit else f"{subj}: {gone=} {hit=}"
        return chk

    def gated_only(level):
        """Expected run verdict for a mutant that breaks only `level` (or the config pin)."""
        return level not in req if level != "pin" else not mode.config_pin

    def sub(name, step, old, new):
        return lambda n, s, c: c.replace(old, new) if (n, s) == (name, step) else c

    try:
        # 0. real files: level map, TRACE vs the real ledger and toml, the real pin file, boot-pin's own self-test
        full = "conformance-full" if "conformance-full" in gates else mode.self_gate
        tr = Trace(TRACE, gates, order, full)  # the real map, judged at the gate that requires C4
        prob = check_map(gates, order, mode, Trace(TRACE, gates, order, mode.self_gate).members()
                         if "C4" in req else ())
        print(f"  {'ok  ' if not prob else 'BAD '} level-map: "
              f"{'every required member, digest and TRACE gate is a gate before ' + mode.self_gate if not prob else prob}")
        if prob:
            bad.append("level-map")
        # TRACE is judged only where C4 is required (as evaluate() does); otherwise its problems are reported, info
        c4 = "C4" in req
        tgood = (not tr.problems and len(tr.rows) == len(tr.ids) > 0) or not c4
        print(f"  {'ok  ' if tgood else 'BAD '} trace-real: spec/TRACE.toml maps {len(tr.rows)}/{len(tr.ids)} ledger "
              f"ids, {len(tr.members())} gates{'' if c4 else ' (C4 not required: info only)'}"
              f"{'; ' + '; '.join(tr.problems[:5]) if tr.problems else ''}")
        if not tgood:
            bad.append("trace-real")
        rp, rprob = load_pins(PINS)
        pdoc = tomllib.load(open(PINS, "rb")) if os.path.isfile(PINS) else {}
        cfgs_ok = all(isinstance(e, dict) and isinstance(e.get("config"), str)
                      and os.path.isfile(os.path.join(ROOT, e["config"])) for e in (pdoc.get("subject") or {}).values())
        pgood = not rprob and set(rp) >= golden and cfgs_ok
        unpinned = sorted(n for n in golden if rp.get(n) is None)
        print(f"  {'ok  ' if pgood else 'BAD '} pins-real: conformance/config-pin.toml lists {sorted(rp)}, configs "
              f"present={cfgs_ok}; not pinned yet (their reports are refused): {unpinned or 'none'}")
        if not pgood:
            bad.append("pins-real")
        bp = subprocess.run([sys.executable, "-I", BOOT_PIN, "--self-test"], capture_output=True, text=True,
                            timeout=300)
        btail = (bp.stdout.strip().splitlines() or [""])[-1]
        bgood = bp.returncode == 0 and btail.startswith("BOOT-PIN SELF-TEST: PASS")
        print(f"  {'ok  ' if bgood else 'BAD '} boot-pin: {btail[:150]}")
        if not bgood:
            bad.append("boot-pin")
            print(bp.stdout[-2000:] + bp.stderr[-1000:])

        # 1. all pass -> PASS; reports valid, signed, verified; required levels 100%
        def all_pass_chk(lines, reports, o, pubs):
            for n, _, prof in SUBJECTS:
                r = reports.get(n)
                if not r:
                    return False, f"{n}: no report"
                for L in mode.gated(prof):
                    if r["levels"][L]["passed"] != r["levels"][L]["total"]:
                        return False, f"{n} {L} not 100%"
                if r["gated"] != mode.gated(prof):
                    return False, f"{n}: gated {r['gated']}"
                if len(r["signatures"]) != 3 or not r["test_keys"]:
                    return False, f"{n}: signatures/test_keys"
                if not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(o, f"{n}.json")):
                    return False, f"{n}.json not written"
                if prof != "module" and (r.get("config_sha256") == pin_vals[n]) != mode.config_pin:
                    return False, f"{n}: config_sha256 {r.get('config_sha256')}"
            if reports["monban-p2"]["levels"].keys() != {"C2"} or "config_sha256" in reports["monban-p2"]:
                return False, "monban-p2 must be C2 only, unpinned"
            c3 = reports["monban-bin-floor"]["levels"]["C3"]
            c4 = reports["monban-bin-floor"]["levels"]["C4"]
            if c3["total"] != len(C3_COMMON) or c4["total"] != len(tr.ids) + 1:
                return False, f"C3 {c3} C4 {c4}"
            return True, (f"3 reports, schema + 3 signatures verified; C3 {c3['passed']}/{c3['total']}, C4 "
                          f"{c4['passed']}/{c4['total']}{', config pinned' if mode.config_pin else ''}")
        reports, o_all, pubs_all = case("all-pass", None, True, check=all_pass_chk)

        # 2. fork subject with tls-client on in cmvp: cmvp-client-policy log fails -> C0 fail
        def tls_client(name, step, c):
            if name == "cmvp-client-policy" and step == "cmd":
                return c.replace("[exit 0]", "CLIENT-POLICY: FAIL (tls client symbols linked in cmvp)\n[exit 1]")
            return c
        case("fork-tls-client-in-cmvp", tls_client, False, subjects=SUBJECTS + [fork],
             check=expect_entry(fork[0], "cmvp-client-policy", "not [exit 0]", level="C0"))

        # 3-8. C0-C2 log rules
        case("missing-log", lambda n, s, c: None if (n, s) == ("budget", "cmd") else c, False,
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-floor", "budget", "log missing", level="C0"))
        case("stale-log", lambda n, s, c: (c, 1_800_000_000 - 60) if (n, s) == ("kx-kat", "cmd") else c, False,
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-cmvp", "kx-kat", "stale", level="C1"))
        case("selftest-fails", sub("mcp-gateway", "selftest", "[exit 0]", "[exit 1]"), False,
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-floor", "mcp-gateway", "selftest log ends", level="C2"))

        def no_run_start(n, s, c):
            if (n, s) == ("layering", "cmd"):
                os.remove(os.path.join(tmp, "no-run-start", "logs", ".run-start"))
            return c
        case("no-run-start", no_run_start, False,
             check=lambda l, r, o, p: (all(x is None for x in r.values()), "no reports without .run-start"))
        # marker without a phase=N line -> nothing is judged, no report
        case("marker-no-phase", None, False, marker_phase_line="",
             check=lambda l, r, o, p: (all(x is None for x in r.values())
                                      and any("no phase=N line" in x for x in l), "no reports without phase=N"))
        # marker names another phase than the toml -> no log of the toml's phase is used
        case("marker-phase-mismatch", None, False, marker_phase_line=f"phase={phase + 1}\n",
             check=lambda l, r, o, p: (all(x is None for x in r.values())
                                      and any(f"phase={phase + 1} run" in x for x in l)
                                      and not any("log fresh" in x for x in l), "other phase's run never judged"))
        case("wrong-cmd-line",
             lambda n, s, c: "$ true\n[exit 0]\n" if (n, s) == ("unsafe-sites", "cmd") else c, False,
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-floor", "unsafe-sites", "does not start with", level="C0"))
        case("ssrf-line-missing", sub("oracles-remote", "cmd", "[ssrf-corpus] SSRF-CORPUS: PASS",
                                      "[ssrf-corpus] SSRF-CORPUS: FAIL"), False,
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-cmvp", SSRF, "lacks a line", level="C2"))

        # 9. artifact digest absent (cmvp) / conflicting (floor) / only in a failing log
        case("digest-absent",
             lambda n, s, c: re.sub(r".*RELEASE-PIPELINE: PASS \(cmvp.*\n", "", c) if s == "cmd" else c, False,
             check=lambda l, r, o, p: (r.get("monban-bin-cmvp") is None and not os.path.exists(
                 os.path.join(o, "monban-bin-cmvp.json")) and r.get("monban-bin-floor") is not None,
                 "cmvp: no digest -> no report, FAIL"))
        case("digest-conflict", sub("release-verify", "cmd", hashlib.sha256(b"floor").hexdigest(), "f" * 64), False,
             check=lambda l, r, o, p: (r.get("monban-bin-floor") is None
                                      and any("conflicting artifact digests" in x for x in l), "floor: conflict"))
        case("digest-from-failing-log", sub("release-rebuild", "cmd", "[exit 0]", "[exit 1]"), False,
             check=lambda l, r, o, p: (r.get("monban-bin-cmvp") is None and r.get("monban-bin-floor")
                                      is not None, "cmvp digest only in a failing log -> no report"))

        # 10. C3: divergence read from the verdict line, not the exit code (oracle: divergence 1 -> C3 red)
        exp3 = gated_only("C3")
        case("c3-select-divergence-1", sub("select-drt", "cmd", ", 0 divergence;", ", 1 divergence;"), exp3,
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-floor", "select-drt", "1 divergence", level="C3"))
        case("c3-token-divergence-1", sub("oracles-local", "cmd", "cases, 0 divergences", "cases, 1 divergences"),
             exp3, check=expect_entry("monban-bin-cmvp", TOKEN, "1 divergences", level="C3"))
        case("c3-write-W2-1", sub("lowering-write-pg", "cmd", " W2=0 ", " W2=1 "), exp3,
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-floor", "lowering-write-pg", "W2=1", level="C3"))
        case("c3-read-leak-1", sub("lowering-read-pg", "cmd", " leak=0 ", " leak=1 "), exp3,
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-floor", "lowering-read-pg", "leak=1", level="C3"))
        case("c3-pdp-fail-verdict-exit0",
             sub("oracles-remote", "cmd", "[pdp-dst] PDP-DST: PASS (40 cases", "[pdp-dst] PDP-DST: FAIL (1 violations"
                 ")\n[pdp-dst] PDP-DST: PASS (40 cases"), exp3,
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-floor", PDP, "FAIL (1 violations", level="C3"))
        case("c3-counter-missing", sub("lowering-read-redis", "cmd", " unrefused=0", ""), exp3,
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-cmvp", "lowering-read-redis", "lacks counter(s) unrefused", level="C3"))
        case("c3-verdict-line-missing",
             lambda n, s, c: re.sub(r"(?m)^LOWERING-WRITE: PASS.*\n", "", c) if (n, s) == ("lowering-write-redis",
                                                                                         "cmd") else c, exp3,
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-floor", "lowering-write-redis", "no `LOWERING-WRITE", level="C3"))
        case("c3-diverge-line", sub("select-drt", "cmd", "PROFILE P-PUBLIC-WEB", "DIVERGE 17  sh 0x11ec vs hrr\n"
                                                                              "PROFILE P-PUBLIC-WEB"), exp3,
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-floor", "select-drt", "DIVERGE line", level="C3"))
        case("c3-stale-drt-log",
             lambda n, s, c: (c, 1_800_000_000 - 5) if (n, s) == ("lowering-read-sqlite", "cmd") else c, exp3,
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-floor", "lowering-read-sqlite", "stale", level="C3"))

        # 11. C4 (oracles: an F1 statement with no TRACE row; a mapped gate without a log from this run)
        exp4 = gated_only("C4")
        tdoc = open(TRACE, encoding="utf-8").read()
        first = tr.ids[0]

        def trace_variant(label, f):
            p = os.path.join(tmp, f"trace-{label}", "spec", "TRACE.toml")
            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)
            with open(p, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                fh.write(f(tdoc))
            shutil.copy(os.path.join(ROOT, LEDGER_REL), os.path.join(os.path.dirname(p), "STATEMENTS.sha256"))
            return p
        row_re = re.compile(rf'(?m)^"{re.escape(first)}" = .*\n')
        case("c4-statement-without-row", None, exp4,
             m=M(trace=trace_variant("norow", lambda t: row_re.sub("", t))),
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-floor", first, "no valid TRACE row", level="C4"))
        case("c4-row-unknown-id", None, exp4,
             m=M(trace=trace_variant("unknown", lambda t: t + '"AegisIR.Nope:AegisIR.Nope.x" = ["proof"]\n')),
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-floor", TRACE_MEMBER, "not a statement id", level="C4"))
        case("c4-gate-not-a-gate", None, exp4,
             m=M(trace=trace_variant("notgate", lambda t: row_re.sub(f'"{first}" = ["proof", "no-such-gate"]\n', t))),
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-cmvp", first, "no valid TRACE row", level="C4", fails=2))
        case("c4-stale-ledger-pin", None, exp4,
             m=M(trace=trace_variant("ledger", lambda t: re.sub(r'ledger_sha256 = "[0-9a-f]+"',
                                                                f'ledger_sha256 = "{"0" * 64}"', t))),
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-floor", TRACE_MEMBER, "re-frozen ledger", level="C4"))
        case("c4-mapped-gate-no-log", lambda n, s, c: None if (n, s) == ("proof", "cmd") else c, exp4,
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-floor", "proof", "log missing", level="C4", fails=len(tr.ids)))
        case("c4-mapped-gate-stale-selftest",
             lambda n, s, c: (c, 1_800_000_000 - 1) if (n, s) == ("select-drt", "selftest") else c,
             exp3 and exp4, check=expect_entry("monban-bin-cmvp", "select-drt", "selftest log stale", level="C3"))
        if "C4" in req:
            later = order[order.index(mode.self_gate) + 1] if order.index(mode.self_gate) + 1 < len(order) else None
            if later:
                case("c4-gate-after-this-gate", None, False,
                     m=M(trace=trace_variant("later", lambda t: row_re.sub(f'"{first}" = ["proof", "{later}"]\n', t))),
                     check=lambda l, r, o, p: (any("runs at or after" in x for x in l) and not r,
                                               f"map refused: {later} runs after {mode.self_gate}"))

        # 12. config pin (oracle: subject booted with a different effective-config hash -> red)
        if mode.config_pin:
            other = hashlib.sha256(b"another config").hexdigest()
            case("pin-different-config-hash", sub("release-verify", "cmd", f"config {pin_vals['monban-bin-floor']}",
                                                   f"config {other}"), False,
                 check=refused("monban-bin-floor", "booted with effective-config hash"))
            case("pin-different-artifact", sub("release-rebuild", "cmd",
                                               f"CONFORMANCE-BOOT: monban-bin-cmvp artifact "
                                               f"{hashlib.sha256(b'cmvp').hexdigest()}",
                                               f"CONFORMANCE-BOOT: monban-bin-cmvp artifact {'e' * 64}"), False,
                 check=refused("monban-bin-cmvp", "is not the judged artifact"))
            case("pin-no-boot-record",
                 lambda n, s, c: re.sub(r"(?m)^CONFORMANCE-BOOT: monban-bin-floor .*\n", "", c), False,
                 check=refused("monban-bin-floor", "no CONFORMANCE-BOOT record"))
            case("pin-conflicting-boots", sub("select-drt", "cmd", "SELECT-DRT: PASS",
                                              f"CONFORMANCE-BOOT: monban-bin-floor artifact "
                                              f"{hashlib.sha256(b'floor').hexdigest()} config {other}\nSELECT-DRT: PASS"),
                 False, check=refused("monban-bin-floor", "booted with effective-config hash"))
            unp = os.path.join(tmp, "pins-unpinned.toml")
            synth_pins(unp, {k: (v if k != "monban-bin-cmvp" else "") for k, v in pin_vals.items()})
            case("pin-unpinned-subject", None, False, m=M(pins=unp),
                 check=refused("monban-bin-cmvp", "no 64-hex config_sha256 pinned"))
            case("pin-boot-in-failing-log", lambda n, s, c: c.replace("[exit 0]", "[exit 1]")
                 if (n, s) == ("release-verify", "cmd") else c, False,
                 check=refused("monban-bin-floor", "no CONFORMANCE-BOOT record"))

        # 13. the same C3 mutant only reports when C3 is not required (the legacy gate's view)
        case("legacy-view-c3-reported", sub("select-drt", "cmd", ", 0 divergence;", ", 1 divergence;"), True,
             m=M(required=LEGACY_REQUIRED, config_pin=False,
                 self_gate="conformance-full" if "conformance-full" in gates else mode.self_gate),
             check=expect_entry("monban-bin-floor", "select-drt", "(reported, not gated)", level="C3"))

        # 14. tamper after signing -> verification fails; one swapped signature -> that alg fails
        names = [n for n, _, _ in SUBJECTS]
        p = os.path.join(o_all, "monban-bin-floor.json")
        r = json.load(open(p))
        r["levels"]["C0"]["passed"] = r["levels"]["C0"]["total"]
        r["gates"][0]["result"] = "pass" if r["gates"][0]["result"] == "fail" else "fail"
        json.dump(r, open(p, "w"), indent=1, sort_keys=True)
        q = os.path.join(o_all, "monban-bin-cmvp.json")
        r2 = json.load(open(q))
        other_r = json.load(open(os.path.join(o_all, "monban-p2.json")))
        r2["signatures"][2] = other_r["signatures"][2]
        json.dump(r2, open(q, "w"), indent=1, sort_keys=True)
        vok, vlines = verify_reports(o_all, names, pubs_all, signer)
        floor_bad = any("monban-bin-floor: signatures ed25519=BAD slh-dsa-sha2-128s=BAD ml-dsa-87=BAD" in x
                        for x in vlines)
        cmvp_bad = any("monban-bin-cmvp: signatures ed25519=ok slh-dsa-sha2-128s=ok ml-dsa-87=BAD" in x for x in vlines)
        p2_ok = any("monban-p2: signatures ed25519=ok slh-dsa-sha2-128s=ok ml-dsa-87=ok" in x for x in vlines)
        good = (not vok) and floor_bad and cmvp_bad and p2_ok
        print(f"  {'ok  ' if good else 'BAD '} tamper-after-signing: floor all 3 BAD={floor_bad}, cmvp swapped "
              f"ml-dsa-87 BAD={cmvp_bad}, untouched p2 verifies={p2_ok}")
        if not good:
            bad.append("tamper-after-signing")
            for l in vlines:
                print("      " + l)
        pubs2, _ = signer.sign([b"x"])
        vok2, vl2 = verify_reports(o_all, ["monban-p2"], pubs2, signer)
        print(f"  {'ok  ' if not vok2 else 'BAD '} other-run-keys: p2 report under a fresh key set "
              f"{'refused' if not vok2 else 'ACCEPTED'}")
        if vok2:
            bad.append("other-run-keys")

        # 15. schema mutants: both validators reject each (incl. the 2026-11-06 additive members)
        base = json.load(open(os.path.join(o_all, "monban-p2.json")))
        base["config_sha256"] = "c" * 64  # exercise the optional member on a signed-shape report
        jran, _ = jsonschema_validate(base)
        muts = {
            "extra-member": lambda x: x.__setitem__("extra", 1),
            "sig-order-swapped": lambda x: x["signatures"].reverse(),
            "two-signatures": lambda x: x["signatures"].pop(),
            "bad-artifact-hex": lambda x: x.__setitem__("artifact_sha256", "A" * 64),
            "level-C5": lambda x: x["levels"].__setitem__("C5", {"passed": 0, "total": 0}),
            "negative-total": lambda x: x["levels"]["C2"].__setitem__("total", -1),
            "result-not-enum": lambda x: x["gates"][0].__setitem__("result", "ok"),
            "missing-log-sha": lambda x: x["gates"][0].pop("log_sha256"),
            "bad-kind": lambda x: x["subject"].__setitem__("kind", "vendor"),
            "v2": lambda x: x.__setitem__("v", 2),
            "sig-not-b64": lambda x: x["signatures"][0].__setitem__("sig", "no t-b64!"),
            "test-keys-str": lambda x: x.__setitem__("test_keys", "true"),
            "bad-date": lambda x: x.__setitem__("generated_at", "yesterday"),
            "config-sha-short": lambda x: x.__setitem__("config_sha256", "c" * 63),
            "config-sha-upper": lambda x: x.__setitem__("config_sha256", "C" * 64),
            "gated-C5": lambda x: x.__setitem__("gated", ["C0", "C5"]),
            "gated-dup": lambda x: x.__setitem__("gated", ["C2", "C2"]),
            "gated-not-array": lambda x: x.__setitem__("gated", "C0-C4"),
        }
        e0 = strict_validate(base)
        _, j0 = jsonschema_validate(base)
        sgood = not e0 and not j0
        missed = []
        for mname, f in muts.items():
            mm = json.loads(json.dumps(base))
            f(mm)
            se = strict_validate(mm)
            ran, je = jsonschema_validate(mm)
            fmt_only = mname == "bad-date" and not jsonschema_checks_datetime()
            if not se or (ran and not je and not fmt_only):
                missed.append(f"{mname} (strict {len(se)}, jsonschema {len(je) if ran else 'n/a'})")
        good = sgood and not missed
        print(f"  {'ok  ' if good else 'BAD '} schema: clean report valid={sgood}{' ' + str(e0 + j0)[:200] if not sgood else ''}, "
              f"{len(muts) - len(missed)}/{len(muts)} mutants rejected by the strict validator"
              f"{' and jsonschema' if jran else ''}{'; missed ' + ', '.join(missed) if missed else ''}")
        if not good:
            bad.append("schema")
    except (RuntimeError, OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as e:
        bad.append(f"error: {e}")
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(tmp, ignore_errors=True)
    n = len(results) + 7  # + level-map, trace-real, pins-real, boot-pin, tamper, other-run-keys, schema
    if bad:
        print(f"CONFORMANCE SELF-TEST: FAIL ({len(bad)} of {n} checks wrong: {', '.join(bad)})")
        return 1
    print(f"CONFORMANCE SELF-TEST: PASS ({n} checks as {mode.self_gate}, required {','.join(mode.required)}"
          f"{' + config pin' if mode.config_pin else ''}: real level map, TRACE, pins and boot-pin ok; all-pass PASS; "
          f"C0-C2 log, digest, C3 divergence, C4 trace{', config-pin' if mode.config_pin else ''} mutants red where "
          f"required; tamper and swapped signature refused; schema mutants rejected)")
    return 0


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="conformance/run")
    ap.add_argument("--logs", default="gates/out/logs")
    ap.add_argument("--out", default="gates/out/conformance")
    ap.add_argument("--toml", default=None)
    ap.add_argument("--gate", default=None)
    ap.add_argument("--require", default=None)
    ap.add_argument("--config-pin", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--self-test", action="store_true")
    a = ap.parse_args()
    a.argv = sys.argv[1:]
    if a.self_test:
        a.toml = a.toml or default_toml(a.logs if os.path.isabs(a.logs) else os.path.join(ROOT, a.logs))
        return self_test(a)
    return main_run(a)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
